  },
  "question": {
    "text": "In a coil of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>, the magnetic flux due to an external magnetic field varies with time as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>. The value of total heat produced in the coil, till the flux becomes zero, will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>It is given that magnetic flux&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>For magnetic flux to be zero&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>According to Faraday&#39;s law of electromagnetic induction,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Heat produced from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}